### Execute batch queries using db.batch

Source: https://github.com/drizzle-team/drizzle-orm-docs/blob/main/src/content/docs/pg/batch-api.mdx

Run multiple SQL statements in a single batch request using the Neon HTTP driver for PostgreSQL. The returned response is strongly typed according to each query in the batch array.

```typescript
const batchResponse = await db.batch([
  db.insert(usersTable).values({ id: 1, name: 'John' }).returning({ id: usersTable.id }),
  db.update(usersTable).set({ name: 'Dan' }).where(eq(usersTable.id, 1)),
  db.query.usersTable.findMany({}),
  db.select().from(usersTable).where(eq(usersTable.id, 1)),
  db.select({ id: usersTable.id, invitedBy: usersTable.invitedBy }).from(usersTable),
]);
```

```typescript
type BatchResponse = [
  { id: number }[],
  NeonHttpQueryResult,
  { id: number; name: string; verified: number; invitedBy: number | null }[],
  { id: number; name: string; verified: number; invitedBy: number | null }[],
  { id: number; invitedBy: number | null }[],
]
```

